+# 01 — Parts and Tools
+
+Approximate Indian market prices (2026); varies by seller/city.
+
+## Electronics
+
+| Part | Qty | Approx ₹ | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| ESP32 DevKit V1 (30-pin) | 1 | 350–500 | WROOM-32, micro-USB or USB-C |
+| BTS7960 43 A H-bridge module | 1 | 250–350 | heatsink included; fuse the input |
+| L298N dual H-bridge module | 1 | 60–100 | with heatsink; remove ENA/ENB jumpers |
+| AHT10 sensor module | 2 | 80–150 ea | fixed I2C address 0x38 → two buses needed |
+| AT24C256 EEPROM module | 1 | 40–80 | 32 kB I2C @0x50 — long-term cycle registry (v2.0.17); A0/A1/A2→GND |
+| Active buzzer module KY-012 | 1 | 10–30 | **mandatory** |
+| Relay module 1-ch, 10 A *(load)* | 1 | 50–100 | opto-isolated; contactor if coil > 10 A |
+| Relay module 1-ch *(bypass)* | 1 | 50–100 | or a contactor for grid bypass |
+| 5 V buck converter (LM2596/mini-360) | 1 | 60–120 | 5 V/2 A to ESP32 from battery rail |
+| Resistor 100 kΩ ¼ W | 1 | ~1 | divider top |
+| Resistor 15 kΩ ¼ W | 1 | ~1 | divider bottom |
+| 2N7000 MOSFET (or NPN+1k) | 1 | 5 | divider pull-down switch |
+| Blade fuse holder + fuse | 1 | 30–50 | sized ~1.25 × coil current |
+| 12 V DC fan (80–120 mm) | 2 | 100–200 ea | one intake, one exhaust |
+| Misc: perfboard, headers, dupont wires, 2.5 mm² wire for power | — | 150–300 | |
+
+## Power (size to your coil — example values)
+
+| Part | Qty | Approx ₹ | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Solar panel 100–330 W | 1 | 2,500–7,000 | 18 V panel for a 12 V system |
+| **Solar charge controller** (PWM/MPPT) | 1 | 500–2,500 | ⚠ many "BMS" boards only protect — they do NOT charge. You need BOTH: charge controller (panel→battery) AND BMS (battery protection), or one combined board |
+| Battery 12 V — **4S LiFePO4 50–100 Ah, ≥50 A BMS recommended** (SLA ok: ≥100 Ah) | 1 | 1,500–6,000 | reliability + longevity: LiFePO4 = 2000+ cycles; 500 W = ~42 A peak |
+| BMS protection board (if bare cells) | 1 | 200–600 | 3S/4S to match pack |
+
+## Heating
+
+| Part | Notes |
+|---|---|
+| Heating coil / nichrome wire | **500 W class: 0.32 Ω** (2 × 1.15 m of 1.0 mm nichrome in parallel). Must match the battery rail voltage |
+| Mica/ceramic former, kanthal supports | coil must not touch chamber walls |
+| Bimetal thermostat 70 °C in series with coil | **hardware safety backstop — do not skip** |
+
+## Chamber & mechanical
+
+- Insulated box (plywood + 25 mm wool/foam, or a steel cabinet) — see 02 §1
+- 2 racks (wire mesh) with ~10 cm clearance below/above
+- Vent pipes 50–63 mm PVC: one low (intake), one high (exhaust) with rain caps
+- Cable glands / grommets where wires enter; electronics mounted OUTSIDE the hot zone
+
+## Tools
+
+- Software side is 100 % free: VS Code/PlatformIO or Arduino IDE 2 —
+  **no paid libraries; not even one library to install** (the firmware is
+  dependency-free; JSON is generated by built-in code)
+- Soldering iron + solder, wire stripper, crimper or pliers
+- Multimeter (compulsory — used in every test step)
+- USB **data** cable for the ESP32 (charge-only cables cause 90 % of "won't upload")
+- Drill, screwdrivers, hot glue / silicone sealant, zip ties
+- Optional: clamp meter (coil current), heat gun (shrink tube)
+
+## Spares worth having
+
+- 1 × ESP32, 1 × AHT10, 5 × fuses, spare dupont wires — the parts that
+  fail first in field use.
